# Timeweb Server Deploy

When the user asks how to update/deploy/pull on the server, always give these exact commands:

```bash
git pull origin main
./deploy.sh
```

`deploy.sh` is a smart script at the project root. It:
- Pulls latest changes
- Detects which files changed (frontend/ vs backend/)
- Rebuilds **only** the affected Docker container(s)

First time on the server only:
```bash
chmod +x deploy.sh
```
